From: DBY-W09 primary port review
Subject: [PATCH DRAFT] dt-bindings: ufs: constrain SM8250 clock-names count

The ROUND54 independent review found that the SM8250-specific branch fixes
the clocks array at exactly eight entries and enumerates eight clock names,
but leaves the clock-names array length inherited from qcom,ufs-common.yaml
(7..9). Add the matching exact count in the SM8250 branch.

Apply this follow-up immediately after ROUND32, before the remaining UFS
binding patches. It is a separate follow-up so the original ROUND32 artifact
and its historical blob identity remain intact.

This is a source-reviewed draft only. No dt_binding_check / dtbs_check or
full-tree application has been run.

---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/ufs/qcom,ufs.yaml | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/ufs/qcom,ufs.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/ufs/qcom,ufs.yaml
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/ufs/qcom,ufs.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/ufs/qcom,ufs.yaml
@@ -165,13 +165,15 @@
         clocks:
           minItems: 8
           maxItems: 8
         clock-names:
+          minItems: 8
+          maxItems: 8
           items:
             - const: core_clk
             - const: bus_aggr_clk
             - const: iface_clk
             - const: core_clk_unipro
             - const: ref_clk
             - const: tx_lane0_sync_clk
             - const: rx_lane0_sync_clk
             - const: rx_lane1_sync_clk
